        "original_id": "a2464f89-527d-5d5d-97dc-469820439d3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Viktor Belenko, John Barron\n- Works: MiG Pilot: The Final Escape of Lieutenant Belenko\n- Events: Viktor Belenko's 1976 defection\n- Places: United States, Hakodate, Japan\n- Products: Mikoyan-Gurevich MiG-25, MiG-25 Foxbat\n\nFacts:\n- Viktor Ivanovich Belenko was born on 15 February 1947.\n- In 1976, former Soviet pilot Viktor Belenko defected to the West while flying a Mikoyan-Gurevich MiG-25 Foxbat jet fighter.\n- Viktor Belenko landed the MiG-25 in Hakodate, Japan during his defection.\n- MiG Pilot: The Final Escape of Lieutenant Belenko is a 1980 biography by John Barron.\n- John Barron's 1980 biography is about Viktor Belenko's life and his 1976 defection to the United States.",
